Synthesis engine (M3) and sequencer (M4) — vendored unmodified in
third_party/eurorack/
  pichenettes/eurorack — Mutable Instruments Plaits (plaits/dsp, resources)
  pichenettes/stmlib — the DSP and utility subset Plaits needs
  Copyright (c) Emilie Gillet — MIT
  https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack
  https://github.com/pichenettes/stmlib
  Licence text: LICENSES/MIT-Mutable-Instruments.txt, and each file's header.
  Commits and the exact file list: third_party/eurorack/README.md.
  firmware/src/sp1_plaits_ui.c adapts Plaits' pot catch-up algorithm
  (plaits/pot_controller.h) and range-mode note mapping (plaits/ui.cc).
  firmware/src/plaits_shim/plaits/user_data.h is ours: it replaces the
  upstream header, which reads STM32 flash.
  firmware/src/plaits_ovr/plaits/dsp/engine/additive_engine.{h,cc} are a
  modified copy of Plaits' additive engine (Emilie Gillet, MIT): the same
  spectrum code, with the partials summed by Clenshaw's algorithm to reduce
  CPU. firmware/src/plaits_ovr/plaits/dsp/fx/ensemble.h and
  .../oscillator/string_synth_oscillator.h are modified copies of Plaits'
  ensemble and string-synth oscillator (Emilie Gillet, MIT), changed only to
  skip work whose result is unused or constant. Other trims (string,
  particle, modal) and two additions to plaits/dsp/voice.{h,cc} -- a
  HARMONICS attenuverter and its internal-envelope routing, which upstream
  Plaits does not have (M4a) -- are applied at build time to
  generated copies of the upstream files, by firmware/CMakeLists.txt; the
  vendored files themselves are not modified.
  Marbles (M4): its random generators
  (marbles/random, marbles/ramp, resources), vendored unmodified in
  third_party/eurorack/marbles, same repository and licence.
  firmware/src/sp1_marbles.cc adapts marbles/marbles.cc's generator code
  and copies its y-divider table; firmware/src/sp1_marbles_scales.inc
  copies the preset scales from marbles/settings.cc; sp1_marbles_ui.c
  copies the loop-length table from marbles.cc and Plaits' pot catch-up.
  The seventh scale slot (sp1_free_scale in sp1_marbles.cc) is ours, written
  in Marbles' own Scale format. Two changes to Marbles are applied at build
  time to generated copies, by firmware/CMakeLists.txt, leaving the vendored
  files unmodified: marbles/random/t_generator.h gains a master-phase setter
  so the clock can start on a beat (M4), and marbles/random/x_y_generator.cc
  has its per-group voltage-range switch redirected so the range can be
  chosen per output channel (M4c) -- the policy behind that is ours, in
  firmware/src/sp1_marbles.cc.
  MIDI (M5a): firmware/src/sp1_midi.cc ports the monophonic note handling of
  Mutable Instruments Yarns from the same eurorack commit -- the mono branches
  of yarns/part.cc (Part::InternalNoteOn/Off, its legato modes and hold
  pedal) and yarns/voice.cc (Voice::NoteOn/Refresh: portamento, with Yarns'
  portamento table in closed form, and pitch bend), and applies Plaits' pot
  catch-up (plaits/pot_controller.h) to MIDI CCs. Nothing from yarns/ is
  vendored. It uses stmlib/algorithms/note_stack.h, vendored unmodified from
  the stmlib commit above. firmware/src/plaits_ovr/plaits/dsp/voice.{h,cc}
  also expose the low-pass gate's state for MIDI (M5a).
  Per upstream's guidelines the name "Mutable Instruments" is not used for
  this derivative work other than as attribution.

