Data inherited from upstream Plaits, redistributed as upstream publishes it
  plaits/dsp/speech/lpc_speech_synth_words.cc describes its word data as "LPC10
  encoded words extracted from various TI ROMs". plaits/resources.cc contains
  the 6-op FM patch banks (syx_bank_0-2); these are linked into the firmware
  even though the 6-op engines are disabled. Upstream publishes both under the
  MIT licence and states no further provenance.

"Teenage Engineering", "SP-1" and "Stem Player" are used only to identify the
hardware this firmware runs on. "Mutable Instruments", "Plaits" and "Marbles"
are used only as attribution.

Nothing in this repository redistributes Teenage Engineering's stock firmware
or bootloader.
